[00:40.00] Hello to the morning moon
[00:43.82] Woke up as you left the room
[00:48.12] Pillows still warm, scent like meadow grass
[00:57.90] Has the feeling come to pass?
[01:01.29] Has the feeling come to stay?
[01:05.35] What can we say?
[01:08.42] Wishing you would hang around
[01:18.36] Living on the waterfront
[01:23.33] Witnessing the gameless hunt
[01:27.57] Mermaids don't kill
[01:30.96] That's the way they sing so fine
[01:35.08] Now your lips are on the line
[01:39.98] Now there is a broken tongue
[01:43.83] Neck is so young
[01:46.49] Felt so frozen
[02:05.57] How you seem to follow through
[02:11.17] On everything you yearned for
[02:15.49] Steps so fair
[02:18.85] So much certainty
[02:22.91] Now as far as we can see
[02:27.17] The water's getting deeper
[02:31.00] My safekeeper
[02:33.97] The wolf is howling for me
[03:09.31] When she holds me in her jaw
[03:13.09] All my blood dripping
[03:16.79] Will I be free to cease gripping?
[03:23.49] Finally laying on the ground
[03:28.71] Open hands empty
[03:32.86] I'll return back again
[03:36.28] If she'll let me